WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome back,
and thank you for being here.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.434
How many times
have you been on our show?

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.734
-I think it's like
third or fourth.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.133
We're like family now.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.901
-As a kid, I always wanted to be
in The Roots, too,

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:09.968
so it just makes me feel closer

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.200
to one of my favorite
rap groups.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.267
-Perfect.
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.701
Thanks for being here.
-Thanks for having me, man.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.033
-You know,
I know you as Killer Mike

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.701
the performer, the artist,

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:22.100
but, also, I never saw
Killer Mike the actor.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.234
And then I watched "Ozark,"
last season of "Ozark,"

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:26.701
and you crushed it, bud.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:29.367
-Man, drug-dealing, white,
middle-class family --

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:32.067
this is my kind of show.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.734
-How did you get
involved with "Ozark"?

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.868
-I loved that show like my old,
white boss loved "The Wire."

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.801
You know, he thought
I was from Baltimore.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.634
So, I was like, "I don't even
have the same accent."

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.968
"But you sold drugs, Michael."

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.133
I met Laura Linney on a plane.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.234
I was stoned.
I was high and high.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.968
And my wife, Shana, used to love
watching "The Big C,"

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.300
so of course I couldn't pass up
a chance to be like,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.501
"My wife loves you."

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:55.601
-Yeah.

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.167
-And she was
just incredibly nice.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:00.100
So, someone on the show
besides her, the director,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.634
who's an
amazing female director,

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.100
called over Jad,
my guy at WME, and say,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.567
"Hey, would Mike
be interested in this?"

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.467
I read the part,
cried tears of joy

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.167
that I got to talk about
"Illmatic" on "Ozark."

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.701
And, man, it just was
a great experience.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.567
-You crushed it.
-I want to be on TV more.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:16.067
-Yeah. I love that you were
high and high.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:20.200
So funny. That's a great line.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.968
You know,
I wanted to ask you about this.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:24.334
Midterm elections coming up.
I know you're an activist.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.534
Is there a message you'd
like to get out there

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.734
to people about
the midterm elections?

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.734
-Yeah, get registered to vote.
Get out and vote.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:32.400
It's very serious
and hyper-serious locally.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.934
On a very local level,
the people that are

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:38.133
your chief of police,
the mayors you elect,

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.033
your prosecutors,
your city-council people.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.200
It's very important.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.000
A couple weeks ago,
they were threatening

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.200
the nightlife in Georgia,
in Atlanta in particular,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.934
which kind of sprouts
some of the biggest artists

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:50.801
in the world, from 2 Chainz
to T.I. to Lil Baby to myself.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.801
And if those clubs,
which a lot are independently

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.400
or small-business owned,
get closed,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.133
then that closes
the whole economy.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:58.467
I got a chance to
go testify with

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.467
a lot of other people
who own the clubs.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:01.801
2 Chainz was there.

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:03.367
And because we did that,
city council

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.868
decided to work with
the club owners

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:05.968
to figure out better policy.

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.133
That's the power of voting

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:08.267
and that's why
I want people to vote.

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:11.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Get out there.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.100
Can we talk about "Run"?
-"Run."

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.033
It's my first single
in 10 years.

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.367
I'm in a very successful rap
group called Run the Jewels.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.968
-Run the Jewels!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:25.234
-Shouts out to El-P,
my guy who's out on Fire Island

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.767
doing what ballin' rappers do,

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.467
as I'm sitting
here dancing and singing.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:29.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:33.200
-And in 10 years,
it felt good to finally say,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.968
"Okay, we take a pause."

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:36.100
COVID said, "Hold on.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.868
Mike, why don't you give
the world a single?"

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.000
And I did it,
and people are responding well.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.634
And it's a hopeful, uplifting,
from Black Atlanta,

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.234
Black America, just to say,

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.167
"We got to keep running
toward victory and freedom."

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.000
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:55.267
And last week,
Governor Newsom signed

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:58.801
the Decriminalizing Artistic
Expression Act in California.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:02:59.968
-Yeah.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.667
-Can you talk about
how important that is?

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:02.968
-So, I'll give you this
really quickly.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.901
There was this really -- She was
an old white lady, right?

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:08.367
She wrote an article called
"How to Kill Your Husband"

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.367
and then she went
and killed her husband.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.334
And after she killed the guy,
the judge said,

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.300
"Well, you can't use the article
she wrote about it,"

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.167
because that's a part of her
artistic expression

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.601
and her First Amendment rights.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.701
Well, a lot of kids
who are poor and in cities

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:22.868
didn't get the same -- or don't
get the same fair treatment.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.434
They could say
something haphazardly

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:26.868
and they could be charged or it
could be added to a charge.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.868
Governor Newsom
and the state of New York --

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:31.968
Assemblymen in California and a
senator, I believe, in New York

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:34.100
both have sponsored bills
to limit

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.467
the law's ability to do that,
because, ultimately,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.100
the Constitution was written
for all of our benefit.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.968
It took the
14th and 15th amendment

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.667
to recognize the
rights of African-Americans,

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.167
but if any of these rights
are infringed upon,

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.834
it will certainly infringe upon
all of us one day.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.868
So I encourage people
to make sure

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:53.000
that you're strict about making
sure your Constitutional rights

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.300
are protected and covered.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.901
And if you don't believe in
freedom of speech

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.567
for those people
you don't agree with,

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.434
you don't believe in
freedom of speech at all.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:00.667
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:09.734
Because, for instance,
you are Killer Mike.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.801
-Yes, yeah.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.501
-But that's not because
you kill people.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:15.968
-Microphones I slaughter.
-Yeah, okay, yeah.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.400
Exactly. Just so you know,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.300
that's exactly kind of
one of the points.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.701
I want to say also, by the way,
thank you for doing this.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:24.801
Your new single, "Run," is out,
and you put it out on cassette.

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:27.534
-Yes.
-That is money.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:30.767
That is money right there.
Why did you do it on cassette?

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:33.167
-So, I've got to shout out
this collector from Atlanta

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.667
named Nuface,
who has cassettes, wax,

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.167
every piece of hip-hop toys.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.400
And he's an amazing
hip-hop historian.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.567
Partly because of people
like him that are out there,

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:44.234
it's value, and I just got
a bunch of old cars.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.200
And my old cars
got CDs and cassettes,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.267
and I like to jam it like

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:48.567
I jammed Raekwon's tape
back in the day.

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:51.868
-That's -- come on.
That's what I'm talking about!

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.033
Killer Mike, everybody.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:56.667
Going to perform "Run" for us
after the break.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:57.968
Come on back, everybody.

